{"ts":1793397535023,"event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103 shipped. (1) libs-shared-contracts PR #1: validateApp now throws when owner is missing/empty (whitespace-only treated as empty); breaking, bumped 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0; CD published 2.0.0 and tagged. (2) apps-sub-route-billing PR #2: passes owner 'payments' (matches package.json team), adopts @mfe/shared-contracts ^2.0.0; CI+CD green. (3) apps-core-shell PR #3: passes owner 'platform', adopts ^2.0.0; CI+CD green. Assumptions: owner value is hardcoded in src/ because the bundler inlines src/ and cannot import package.json, so it mirrors the package.json team field and can drift if team changes; the owner check treats whitespace-only as empty; no change to the registry range of 1.x consumers since 2.x was a breaking release and the apps were moved explicitly."}
